1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,249
Are Twitch's free clip tools enough?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,865
It depends how much of the stream you want clipped.

3
00:00:06,865 --> 00:00:12,423
Twitch's "Clip That" grabs the last 60 seconds, and Auto Clips is still in limited testing.

4
00:00:12,423 --> 00:00:17,553
To get the whole stream ranked into captioned clips, pick an AI clipper like ClipMe.

5
00:00:18,503 --> 00:00:21,388
Twitch's tools are free and great for one moment.

6
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:24,626
ClipMe ranks the whole stream and cuts captioned clips.

7
00:00:25,575 --> 00:00:31,164
It reads Twitch chat, and chat activity is one of the signals ClipMe uses to rank each moment.

8
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:37,427
Every clip comes out captioned in 9:16, and Pro adds 4:5 and 1:1.

9
00:00:38,377 --> 00:00:41,823
If you only need one quick clip, keep the free tools.

10
00:00:41,823 --> 00:00:45,268
For the whole stream, paste a VOD free at clipme.com.

